---
// The install doc's fresh-install section: the weekly installers, and how
// to check one. One column: it lives in the docs' reading column.
import DownloadRow from './DownloadRow.astro';
import { COSIGN_PUB, ISOS, REPO } from '../data/site';

const SUMS = ['sha256', 'sha256.sig', 'json'];

// The signature covers the checksum manifest, not the 5GB ISO -- verifying
// the manifest and then checking the ISO against it proves the same thing
// without cosign reading five gigabytes. --insecure-ignore-tlog is the
// documented flag for plain key-based verification: the trust anchor here is
// the published key, not a transparency-log entry, and the name is cosign's,
// not a warning about this page.
const VERIFY = [
  `cosign verify-blob ${ISOS.vanilla}.sha256`,
  `--key ${COSIGN_PUB}`,
  `--signature ${ISOS.vanilla}.sha256.sig`,
  '--insecure-ignore-tlog=true',
  `&& sha256sum -c ${ISOS.vanilla}.sha256`,
].join(' ');

const shown = [
  `cosign verify-blob ${ISOS.vanilla}.sha256 \\`,
  `  --key ${COSIGN_PUB} \\`,
  `  --signature ${ISOS.vanilla}.sha256.sig \\`,
  '  --insecure-ignore-tlog=true \\',
  `&& sha256sum -c ${ISOS.vanilla}.sha256`,
].join('\n');
---

<div class="iso">
  <p class="lede">
    Each variant gets an installer ISO every week, built from the published image. It boots
    into Pulsar's own installer: pick a disk, set a passphrase, and the next thing you see is
    Pulsar's first boot. The checksums are signed with Pulsar's release&nbsp;key.
  </p>

  <div class="grid">
    <div>
      <ul class="isos">
        <DownloadRow which="standard" file={ISOS.vanilla} sums={SUMS} />
        <DownloadRow which="nvidia" file={ISOS.nvidia} sums={SUMS} />
      </ul>
      <p class="hint">
        Write it to a USB&nbsp;stick with GNOME&nbsp;Disks or <code>dd</code> and boot from&nbsp;it.
        The <code>.json</code> file next to each ISO has the digest of the image it installs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class="cap">
        <span>The private half of the release key never leaves the signing&nbsp;host.</span>
      </p>
      <arc-code-block
        class="theme-fixed-dark"
       
        language="bash"
        filename="verify"
        code={shown}
        data-copy={VERIFY}
      ></arc-code-block>
      <p class="hint">
        The public half is published next to the ISOs and committed to the repo as{' '}
        <code>keys/cosign.pub</code>. Every signature is checked against the committed copy before
        anything is published. ISOs published before November 9, 2026 were signed with an earlier
        key, kept as{' '}
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/keys/cosign-before-2026-11-09.pub`}><code>keys/cosign-before-2026-11-09.pub</code></a>.
      </p>
      <p class="hint"><code>--insecure-ignore-tlog</code> skips Rekor, Sigstore’s public transparency log. The ISOs’ signatures aren’t logged there yet (the images’ are), so this check rests on the published key alone.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    /* explicit, or the implicit column sizes to the longest filename */
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .isos {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .cap {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  arc-code-block {
    display: block;
  }
  .hint {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
